producing working code to accomplish a task. But&nbsp;
that code is still untrusted and it can't be run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:08.800
inside the same environment that has access&nbsp;
to our production systems. We need a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:08.800 --> 00:25:14.000
production grade environment that's designed&nbsp;
for executing untrusted code in a secure and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:20.480
isolated way. Vercel is actually no stranger to&nbsp;
this problem of untrusted code execution because&nbsp;&nbsp;

